{"name":"Camembert","hex":"#fbf3df","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Camembert","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A village in Normandy, France, famous for being the place where camembert cheese was invented."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Camembert"}],"entries":[{"title":"Camembert","blocks":[{"text":"Camembert is a moist, soft, creamy, surface-ripened cow's milk cheese. It was first made in the late 18th century in Camembert, Normandy, in northwest France. It is sometimes compared in look, taste and texture to brie cheese, albeit with a slightly lower butterfat content than brie's typical 20–25% by weight."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Camembert_de_Normandie_%28AOP%29_11.jpg/330px-Camembert_de_Normandie_%28AOP%29_11.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Camembert"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Camembert.JPG/500px-Camembert.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Camembert.JPG/1280px-Camembert.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Camembert.JPG/500px-Camembert.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Camembert from Normandy","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACamembert.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Camembert_cheese_selection_at_a_supermarket_in_F%C3%A9camp%2C_Normandy.jpg/500px-Camembert_cheese_selection_at_a_supermarket_in_F%C3%A9camp%2C_Normandy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Camembert_cheese_selection_at_a_supermarket_in_F%C3%A9camp%2C_Normandy.jpg/1280